Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:58:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix four hardcoded-year issues found by review, add
 regression guard

Supports Next Season Data Release Checklist item 1 (update the season
map) by making the remaining places that didn't already derive from
SEASONS do so:

- Sources/Notes media-guide citation now calls media_guide_source_context()
  instead of a literal 2026 URL.
- Both game-note boilerplate-stripping regexes (season-footer line,
  "SINGLE-GAME HIGHS" trailer) now match any four-digit year instead of
  a literal 2026.
- The note-category classifier's "season" match now matches any
  four-digit year instead of a literal 2026.
- README.txt prose describing the roster/stat download and career-stat
  copy output now describes the season range generically instead of
  naming 2025/2026, so it doesn't go stale when SEASONS is updated.

Added tests/test_hardcoded_season_years.py: failing-first coverage for
each fix (built from a monkeypatched future season year, not just the
literal 2026 fixtures), plus a regression guard that scans src/*.py for
any bare season-year literal outside a documented allowlist (the SEASONS
definition line, and the AUSL Draft Results URL, which is a specific
already-published article link that must be updated manually each
season rather than derived).

